<h1>right-threaded tree</h1>
<p>
(data structure)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A variant of a <a href="threadedtree.html"><em>threaded tree</em></a> in which only the right thread, i.e. <a href="link.html"><em>link</em></a> to the successor, of each <a href="node.html"><em>node</em></a> is maintained.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Generalization</strong> (I am a kind of ...)<br>
<a href="threadedtree.html"><em>threaded tree</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="binarySearchTree.html"><em>binary search tree</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
Keeping only the right thread, rather than both left and right threads, keeps it quick to find the next greater key and faster to insert and delete.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
Ben Pfaff's  <a href="https://adtinfo.org/" target="_blank">explanations and code (C)</a>

